  "question": "The heating company needs to manage information about its users and their heat supply status. Each user has an ID, name, address, and contact information. For each heat supply instance, the supply date, supply quantity, user ID, and operator ID need to be recorded. Each operator has an ID, name, department, and contact information.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0054\nCREATE TABLE `operator` (\n  `operator_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `operator_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `department` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `contact_info` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`operator_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `contact_info` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `heat_supply` (\n  `supply_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `supply_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `supply_quantity` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `operator_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`supply_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `heat_supply_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `heat_supply_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`operator_id`) REFERENCES `operator` (`operator_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
